==============================================================================
S669 equinumerosity versus outer-extension usability
==============================================================================

Source anchors
  Friedman official pages: homeomorphic embeddings, internal finite tree embeddings, finite functions / large cardinals, invariant maximality.
  Royle et al.: tournaments and even graphs are equinumerous.
  Topology anchor: cardinality does not preserve dimension/homeomorphism; deletion/link profiles are finite shadows.

A. Equal-cardinality Euclidean toy
  line_P27       dim=1 |V|=27 degree=((1, 2), (2, 25)) deletion=((1, 2), (2, 25)) profile=(('P3', True), ('branch3', False), ('branch5', False), ('C4', False), ('puncture_splits', True), ('max_ball2', 5))
  plane_3x9      dim=2 |V|=27 degree=((2, 4), (3, 16), (4, 7)) deletion=((1, 27),) profile=(('P3', True), ('branch3', True), ('branch5', False), ('C4', True), ('puncture_splits', False), ('max_ball2', 11))
  space_3x3x3    dim=3 |V|=27 degree=((3, 8), (4, 12), (5, 6), (6, 1)) deletion=((1, 27),) profile=(('P3', True), ('branch3', True), ('branch5', True), ('C4', True), ('puncture_splits', False), ('max_ball2', 19))

  Interpretation: all three carriers have the same finite cardinal shadow |V|=27.
  The 1D carrier is puncture-disconnected; 2D/3D are not.  Degree and growth profiles separate all three.

B. Usability audit for the dimension predicate
channel                        groups  mixed max_bucket
cardinality                         1      1          3
cardinality+deletion                2      1          2
cardinality+degree                  3      0          1
growth_profile                      3      0          1
small_embedding_profile             3      0          1
  Reading: cardinality alone has one mixed bucket containing dimensions 1,2,3.
  Deletion repairs the 1D-vs-higher split but still mixes 2D/3D; local growth or embedding profiles repair the toy completely.

C. Outer-extension check
  extension operation=add an outer layer while preserving the internal carrier type
  line_P27       -> line_P29       |V| 27->29 dim=1 full_profile_changed=False dimension_signature_changed=False
  plane_3x9      -> plane_5x9      |V| 27->45 dim=2 full_profile_changed=True dimension_signature_changed=False
  space_3x3x3    -> space_5x3x3    |V| 27->45 dim=3 full_profile_changed=True dimension_signature_changed=False
  Reading: extension changes raw size and sometimes boundary/growth counts.
  The dimension signature remains stable, which is the usability coordinate the cardinal shadow lacked.

D. Royle/even-graph count shadow, imported from S617
   n       graphs  tournaments  degree_even   naive_even
   3            4            2            2            2
   4           11            4            3            7
   5           34           12            7           22
   6          156           56           16          100
