  12 165091172592 154108311168            -  10982861424
  S617 finding: degree-even and naive Burnside-even are not the Royle-even theorem.
  Even when a true equinumerous class exists, HYP-2187 still asks for a fiber functor preserving H/beta1/packet data.
  H splits by beta1 in the stored audit:
    n=5: {9: [0, 1]}
    n=6: {17: [0, 1], 23: [0, 1], 33: [0, 1], 37: [0, 1], 45: [0, 1]}

E. S668 Friedman-tree compatibility
  S668 finite-tree target=contains rooted homeomorphic color chain 0 -> 1 -> 2.
  Coarse channels leaked: size_height mixed=6, color_hist=10, frontier=46, raw outer_address=55.
  Embedding channels repaired: small_embedding_profile=0, full_embedding_profile=0, address_plus_small_embedding=0 mixed fibers.
  S669 reading: cardinal/count equality is exactly the wrong level for outer-extension theorem transfer.

F. Tournament Analysis over transfer channels
  vertices=proof-transfer channels
  observable=(cardinal fidelity, extension purity, dimension retention, tournament fiber retention, Friedman embedding fit, actionability)
  switch=majority; tie Hamiltonian path=listed priority order
  score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1, 7: 1}
  directed_3cycles=0
